# Omarchy core package list pacstrapped by the ISO.
# The ISO builder also reads this file when constructing the offline mirror.
#
# Every name here must exist under exactly this name on BOTH official Arch
# x86_64 and archlinux32 i686: the list is shared and pacstrap aborts on a
# target it cannot find. Verified with `pacman -Si` in both chroots.
#
# NOT IN THIS LIST, ON PURPOSE: Hyprland itself and the hypr* libraries it
# links. Omarchy CPU runs this fork's Hyprland and aquamarine, which add the
# pixman (CPU) renderer that upstream does not have, so the compositor cannot
# come from a repo:
#
#   Hyprland      github.com/cederikdotcom/Hyprland, branch pixman-renderer
#   aquamarine    github.com/cederikdotcom/aquamarine, branch cpu-backend
#
# Both are installed from the fork build until a fork package repo exists;
# see docs/runbooks/install-x86_64.md and docs/runbooks/a1181-install.md.
# The same goes for their hypr* dependencies (hyprutils, hyprlang, hyprcursor,
# hyprgraphics, hyprwayland-scanner): official Arch x86_64 carries all of them
# at the versions Hyprland 0.56 wants, but archlinux32 has hyprcursor and
# hyprgraphics not at all and hyprutils/hyprlang far too old, so the fork build
# provides them on both arches rather than the list installing two different
# stacks. Everything below is the shared runtime the fork binaries link
# against, and that a repo package would have pulled in for us.
#
# NOT IN THIS LIST FOR THE SAME REASON: quickshell, which draws the Omarchy
# desktop (bar, menu, notifications, OSD, wallpaper, lock screen, tray and the
# whole plugin system under shell/). Upstream installs it from
# pkgs.omarchy.org; it is in neither official Arch nor archlinux32, so a tester
# builds it from source:
#
#   quickshell   github.com/quickshell-mirror/quickshell, tag v0.3.1
#
# Build commands, per arch, are in docs/runbooks/install-x86_64.md and
# docs/runbooks/a1181-install.md. Quickshell links PRIVATE Qt APIs and must be
# rebuilt whenever qt6-base or qt6-declarative is upgraded, or it crashes on an
# ABI mismatch -- so pin those two if you are not prepared to rebuild.
#
# The qt6-* entries below, plus jemalloc, glib2, libxcb and wayland, are that
# build's RUNTIME dependencies. Its build-only dependencies (cmake, ninja,
# pkgconf, cli11, qt6-shadertools, spirv-tools, wayland-protocols and
# vulkan-headers -- headers only, there is no runtime Vulkan requirement) are
# deliberately absent: they belong on the build host, not on a MacBook.
# libgbm, which quickshell's screencopy needs, comes from mesa on both arches.

